Autonomous Intelligence Looping (Sequence Architecture)
 * Phase 1: Telemetry Ingestion & Air-Gap Sensing: High-frequency Hall-effect position sensors capture sub-micron radial and axial rotor displacements across the active magnetic levitation array.
 * Phase 2: Closed-Loop Flux Adjustment: Real-time neural inference engines process sensor streams to dynamically modulate electromagnetic flux, maintaining a zero-contact physical state.
 * Phase 3: Fluid Film Viscosity Modulation: Telemetry signals evaluate load spikes, instructing active micro-valves to tune pressure within the redundant fluid film bearing interface.
 * Phase 4: Surface Integrity Verification: Continuous acoustic emission monitoring evaluates the boundary friction state and micro-wear rates across the diamond-like carbon (DLC) nano-coating.
 * Phase 5: Autonomous State Commit: Cryptographic ledgers record execution metrics and adjust predictive control parameters for subsequent rotational cycles.
